'''Glitch2''' is a [[Common Weapons|common]] knife that was originally thought to be the non-duplicated version of [[Glitch1]]. However, in a JD [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GuQ_XAnuXGg video], they claimed that Glitch2 was originally a Black Luger, which was duplicated by a hacker. [[Nikilis]] subsequently transformed them into what is now known as Glitch2. 

==Appearance==
The whole knife uses a white shade, except the handle is slightly darker. If you equip Glitch2, it will be in a weird orientation on your back/waist. 

==Trivia==
*Despite this knife being named Glitch2, it is thought to be the first ever Glitch to be added into [[Murder Mystery 2]].
*Allegedly, this knife is a Black Luger from the [[Christmas Event 2015|2015 Christmas Event]], which explains why this was the first ever Glitch to be added.
*This knife has a weird orientation on your back/waist when you equip it, and, for non-[[Radio Gamepass|radio gamepass]] owners, makes it kind of look like the player owns the pass.
*Glitch2 used to be named Glitch and did not stack with the other Glitch, now known as [[Glitch1]]. This issue was later fixed on January 24th, 2023 when Nikilis changed the names of the Glitches to Glitch1 and Glitch2 to differentiate them from one another.

